INSERT INTO `node` VALUES
(1,1,'article','fd48c9bf-1c36-4033-804b-5c8bf8c0e685','en'),
(2,2,'article','dd72549b-4b83-461f-be51-65aacf11c387','en'),
(3,3,'article','354a18cc-8bf1-448a-9a6d-06528e7d6354','en'),
(4,4,'article','f01eee20-98c7-45e0-a160-1419fa94ba12','en'),
(5,5,'article','e152b6aa-07b6-448a-aea2-d8bdd02935b5','en'),
(6,6,'page','d5c8e13d-56ca-4815-9ddf-6088dffbdd0b','en');
INSERT INTO `node__body` VALUES
('article',0,1,1,'en',0,'<p>Drupal is a powerful content management system that organises information into entities. A node represents a piece of content, while a taxonomy term provides classification through a vocabulary.</p>\n<p>Site builders extend Drupal by enabling a module. A theme controls visual presentation, and Twig drives the templates that render each page. Behind the scenes, Symfony components handle routing, the HTTP kernel and dependency injection.</p>\n<p>When code needs to react to events, developers attach a hook. When swappable behaviour is required, they implement a plugin. Configuration is exported as YAML so the same setup can be shared between environments.</p>',NULL,'basic_html'),
('article',0,2,2,'en',0,'<p>Performance in Drupal relies on layered caching. Every render array is wrapped with a cache tag and one or more cache context entries. When content changes, Drupal invalidates only the tags it must, instead of clearing everything.</p>\n<p>The Filter system caches the formatted output of each text field per format. Pages are then assembled from those cached fragments by the render pipeline. This is why even a complex page with many entities can still be served in milliseconds.</p>\n<p>For dynamic data, a service can be marked cacheable through its metadata, and Drupal will compose the right cache keys from the surrounding context.</p>',NULL,'basic_html'),
('article',0,3,3,'en',0,'<p>A modern Drupal module begins as a Composer package. Composer resolves third-party libraries, including those provided by Symfony, and integrates them into the autoloader.</p>\n<p>Inside the module, a service is declared in YAML and wired together by dependency injection. The service can then be reused by a controller, a plugin, a filter or a queue worker, without any of them having to know how it was built.</p>\n<p>Because the configuration of services lives outside the code, the same module can be plugged into different projects with minimal changes.</p>',NULL,'basic_html'),
('article',0,4,4,'en',0,'<p>A migration moves data from a legacy source into the Drupal entity system. Source rows are mapped to fields on a node, taxonomy term or any other entity. The Migrate API is itself implemented as a plugin family.</p>\n<p>Once content lands in Drupal, editorial workflows take over. A vocabulary may classify the imported items, and a render array describes how each one is displayed.</p>\n<p>Configuration related to the migration — source plugins, process pipelines, destinations — is exported as configuration so it can be reviewed and re-run.</p>',NULL,'basic_html'),
('article',0,5,5,'en',0,'<p>A filter transforms text after it has been authored but before it is rendered. Drupal ships with filters that sanitise HTML, convert URLs into links, and align embedded images. Custom filters can highlight glossary words, blur sensitive data, or rewrite shortcodes.</p>\n<p>Because the filter result is cached per format, even an expensive transformation runs only when content actually changes. This makes filters a natural place to add editorial helpers without slowing down delivery.</p>',NULL,'basic_html'),
('page',0,6,6,'en',0,'<p>Drupal is a powerful content management system that organises information into entities. A node represents a piece of content, while a taxonomy term provides classification through a vocabulary.</p><p>Site builders extend Drupal by enabling a module. A theme controls visual presentation, and Twig drives the templates that render each page. Behind the scenes, Symfony components handle routing, the HTTP kernel and dependency injection.</p><p>When code needs to react to events, developers attach a hook. When swappable behaviour is required, they implement a plugin. Configuration is exported as YAML so the same setup can be shared between environments.</p>','','basic_html');
